  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "LJpegDecompressor::decode",
    "file": "librawspeed/src/librawspeed/decompressors/LJpegDecompressor.cpp",
    "description": "Root cause is insufficient validation of tile offsets in LJpegDecompressor::decode(): it only checks offsetX/offsetY against image dimensions, but does not validate that offsetX + decoded frame width (and component expansion) stays within the allocated row stride. decodeN<4>() then computes dest from getDataUncropped(offX,destY) and writes N_COMP samples per pixel in a loop (*dest++ at line ~135), causing out-of-bounds write when crafted JPEG frame metadata and offsets make width calculation inconsistent with real writable buffer extent.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzer supplies a RawImage plus 3 u32 values (offsetX, offsetY, fixDng16Bug) followed by JPEG data. With offsetX/offsetY individually in-range but near boundary, and SOF/SOS parameters selecting 4-component decode path, decodeScan()->decodeN<4>() performs writes based on frame.w and computed width from (cpp*(dim.x-offX))/N_COMP. Missing holistic bounds check in LJpegDecompressor::decode allows a crafted stream to reach decodeN and trigger wild write at line 135."
  },
